    "title": "Jaylen Brown's \"Fake Hairline\" Strikes Again After Rubbing Off On Wizards Forward's White Jersey [VIDEO] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kenny Nosay ,\n36 minutes ago\nJaylen Brown (Image Credit: Imagn) Jaylen Brown’s fake hairline has been shoved into the spotlight ever since he accidentally tainted OG Anunoby’s jersey a couple of weeks ago. Then, the same incident happened when the Celtics clashed against Detroit. This time, the victim was Ronald Holland II.\nApparently, Brown doesn’t want to go bald. He made sure of that thought when he called LeBron James and asked whether a trip to Turkey to fix his hair was worth it. Fans went wild with their reactions to that one . Now, the one-time champ’s fake hairline has struck again, and this time, it’s against the Washington Wizards.\nWhen Brown drove at the top of the key, he collided with Washington Wizards forward Kyshawn George. His head hit George’s shirt, immediately tainting it with ink. The clip has been shared on X by ‘Fullcourtpass.’\nThe refs called Brown for an offensive foul on the play. What’s worse is that a few Wizards players gathered around George to view the black spot on his undersleeves. The youngster’s face after the collision speaks volumes.\nJaylen Brown Flooded With Hair Transplant Offers Jaylen Brown (Image Credits: Imagn) While balding is an inevitable process for some guys, the 29-year-old hasn’t embraced the fate of his hair yet. After his painted-on hairline was exposed, he’s been seeking advice on how to grow it back. He even went as far as to admit his balding struggles on social media.\nBut if there’s a silver lining to all the hairline-related jokes Brown has received, TMZ reported that the Celtics forward has been flooded with hair transplant offers from multiple US-based doctors. He may be pressed to find a time for the procedure because the 2025-2026 season has just started.\nMight as well wait when Boston’s season is over, and he could get things done by that time. For now, he may have to stick with his painted-on hairline if he wants to look good on the court.\nThe post originally published on .",
